@endnode
@node Tooltypes "Available ToolTypes"

OVERRIDE_LEVEL=<LEVEL>
----------------------------------------------------------------------
iE. 
OVERRIDE_LEVEL=200, this means every User with Level 200 or higher
are disabled from the Duplicate Check Procedure.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

NAME.<#>=<String>
----------------------------------------------------------------------
iE.
NAME.1=ByteAndi/MST
NAME.2=Dr.Dre!/tRSi
NAME.3=Jeannie/SR
This means all Users above are disabled from the Duplicate Check
Procedure.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

DISPLAY_TXT (Optional)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
If you set this ToolType, the FastDupe will search in the actual
Conference for an TextFile called FASTDUPE.TXT(.GR) if the (.GR) not
found then it will display the .TXT File.
Here you can write down what ever you want.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

DOORSTART.<#>=<STRING>
----------------------------------------------------------------------
About this ToolType it is possible to start up to 10 other Doors/Tools 
after each DupeCheck, this is usefull if you run the ConfTop from bObO
or the FileSystem for the BossNuke or whatever you run after each Upload.
Explainment of the ToolType:
DOORSTART.1=FASTDUPE1
This means the FASTDUPE trys to execute the FASTDUPE1.Info in 
BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ or BBS:COMMANDS/Node<X>CMD/
Build in this Icon what ever you want to run after the Upload.
See our Example Icon from the original Archive.
I hope this will explain a bit this ToolType.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                     @{" Main Menu " Link main}
@endnode
